option to evaluate. The update follows e2e-assures earlier work on UK focused security tooling.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:15.220
Okay, let's pop the hood on the million token context claims in these new MOE models.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:21.280
Everyone talks about million token context as if it is simply a bigger KV cache.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:26.840
In practice, it requires coordinated changes across attention, residual connections,

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:31.120
and optimizer to keep both memory and compute manageable.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:38.720
DeepSeq V4's hybrid CSA plus HCA approach compresses the attention computation so

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:46.900
that a 1 million token forward pass uses only 27% of the flops and 10% of the KV cache of the prior

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:53.240
version. The manifold constrained hyperconnections further stabilized training at this scale by replacing

00:07:53.240 --> 00:08:00.880
standard residuals with learned manifold projections. At inference time, the savings only appear once

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:08.340
context exceeds roughly 128,000 tokens. Below that, the overhead of the compressed paths can

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:14.560
actually slow things down. Teams should therefore profile both short and long contexts before

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:20.220
committing to these architectures. The practical decision rule is simple. If your typical

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:26.800
agent session stays under 100,000 tokens, the new mechanisms add complexity with little payoff.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:32.300
Once you routinely exceed that threshold, the efficiency gains become decisive.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:41.540
Test DeepSeq V4 Flash or V4 Pro on hugging phase for any workflow that already pushes past 128,000

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:49.440
tokens and measure actual KV cache and latency savings. Run the data set apps OneLiners from Simon

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:56.720
Willison's post to prototype a small HTML plus JS app backed by a real relational database in under

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:03.980
five minutes. Review andthropics project fetch phase two blog for concrete numbers on how much faster

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:10.280
frontier models now iterate on robotics code compared with human teams. Experiment with liquid

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:18.220
AI's 350 million Colbert retriever on Edge hardware if you need fast multilingual search without

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:25.380
calling larger cloud models. More inference providers are expected to add GLM 5.2 support

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:32.460
following Simon Willison's request to GROC and Sarabras. Additional phase two project fetch results

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:38.440
from Anthropic will likely include more detailed failure analysis and iteration metrics.

